cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Reconstructing Flanders: an evidence-first, machine-assisted reconstruction
  of Flemish families from parish and civil registers
message: >-
  If you use this method, the tooling, or the data, please cite it. If you use
  the harvested records, cite the archives that hold them and Open Archives,
  which publishes their indexes as open data.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Bundervoet
    given-names: Shaun
abstract: >-
  A working method for reconstructing families from Flemish parish and civil
  registers with every link traceable to its supporting document. Combines
  event-indexed harvesting of archive indexes, blocking and rarity-weighted
  record linkage in the Fellegi-Sunter tradition, and an adversarial
  verification loop in which a dedicated agent attempts to refute each proposed
  identity before it is accepted. Negative results — searches that found
  nothing, candidates that were refuted — are retained as first-class data, and
  verifier rulings accumulate as a labelled pair set for calibrating the linkage
  thresholds.
keywords:
  - genealogy
  - record linkage
  - historical demography
  - family reconstitution
  - Flanders
  - Belgium
  - parish registers
  - entity resolution
  - Fellegi-Sunter
